    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0875" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–2848: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-28T11:00:00+08:00">October 28, 1948—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 28—12:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>309. If Embassy approves issuance restrained statements suggested Peiping
                    telegram 594 to Embassy,<anchor n="26" xml:id="d771-f1"/> we suggest statement
                    be prepared <pb facs="0876" n="866" xml:id="pg866"/> by Embassy and text sent
                    Tientsin and Peiping for simultaneous release. Such action would preclude
                    possible confusion arising from issuance respective offices of different
                    statements.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 552, repeated Department 309.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d771-f1" n="26" xml:id="d771-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Department as telegram No. 396, October 27, 5 p.m., above.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
